1
00:00:01,417 --> 00:00:04,253
- "Previously on The Mentalist..."
- "Yeah, Lena's on a short list"

2
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:07,173
for a position in the Commerce
Department in D.C. so we're celebrating.

3
00:00:07,298 --> 00:00:08,341
It's not a done deal yet.

4
00:00:08,466 --> 00:00:10,134
I have to be confirmed,
and that could take months.

5
00:00:10,259 --> 00:00:12,970
What can you tell me
about Rio Bravo station?

6
00:00:13,095 --> 00:00:15,556
- "I don't think I want to go to D.C."
- Why?

7
00:00:15,681 --> 00:00:17,266
Because you're gonna be
asked questions

8
00:00:17,391 --> 00:00:20,102
and if any of those questions
involve Rio Bravo

9
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:22,897
then you need to be able to say
that you don't know anything about it.

10
00:00:28,819 --> 00:00:30,071
{\an8}"Hi, folks.
Welcome to Alamo Brewhouse."

11
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:31,614
"Christine will show you
to your table."

12
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:33,658
Hey, guys. Come on and join us.

13
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:36,661
We have a great Chilean sea bass
today for you guys.

14
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,287
Sit you right over here.

15
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:53,010
D.E.A.! Search warrant!

16
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:55,096
- Come on, let me see some hands!
- Put your hands on the table!

17
00:00:56,305 --> 00:00:57,598
D.E.A.!
"Police! Police!"

18
00:00:57,723 --> 00:01:00,268
- Down on the ground now!
- Head down on the ground now!

19
00:01:01,143 --> 00:01:02,395
Hands behind your head!

20
00:01:02,853 --> 00:01:04,564
- Sit!
- What's going on?

21
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:06,941
We have a warrant to search
these premises for illegal narcotics.

22
00:01:07,066 --> 00:01:08,442
Narcot...
This is a restaurant.

23
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:10,695
Sir, read the warrant.
Let me do my job, okay?

24
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,238
You want a meeting with me?
Let's go talk in my office.

25
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:13,406
- Oh, you wanna go to your office?
- Let's talk.

26
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:15,032
Yeah, let's do that.
Let's start there.

27
00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:22,373
What do you got, Orosco?

28
00:01:22,498 --> 00:01:25,209
Yeah, we searched the office,
dining room, freezer.

29
00:01:25,334 --> 00:01:27,545
K9 went through everything.
We got nothing.

30
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:30,006
- Okay, search again.
- Okay.

31
00:01:30,631 --> 00:01:31,674
Don't walk away.
I'm talking to you.

32
00:01:31,799 --> 00:01:33,718
Mr. Korbell, we are going
to finish our search.

33
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:34,885
This is harassment!

34
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,512
The more you interfere,
the longer it's gonna take.

35
00:01:36,637 --> 00:01:37,972
Who's going to clean
this place up? Huh?

36
00:01:38,889 --> 00:01:40,558
- I'm talking to you, bitch!
- Hey! Hey!

37
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:43,728
Okay.

38
00:01:44,729 --> 00:01:46,230
Don't talk to my agent
that way.

39
00:01:48,357 --> 00:01:49,400
Okay, easy.

40
00:01:50,484 --> 00:01:51,527
Gonzalez.

41
00:01:58,701 --> 00:02:00,411
Pack up and get out of here.

42
00:02:01,912 --> 00:02:02,955
I'm watching you, pal.

43
00:02:03,581 --> 00:02:05,041
Little dog, put your hands on me?

44
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:21,015
Excuse me.
I'm looking for Bill Peterson.

45
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:22,391
There he is right there.

46
00:02:24,143 --> 00:02:25,353
- Hey!
- Hey.

47
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,690
Dennis. You look good.

48
00:02:30,274 --> 00:02:32,318
- You lost weight.
- Oh, yeah, a little bit. Thanks.

49
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:34,945
- How's Lena?
- She's in D.C.

50
00:02:35,404 --> 00:02:36,489
Big things doing.

51
00:02:36,739 --> 00:02:37,865
- Really?
- Oh, yeah.

52
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:39,408
Oh, good for her.

53
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:44,705
So, Dennis Abbott is handling
the After Action report

54
00:02:44,830 --> 00:02:48,250
on my team's failed raid
on Alamo Brewhouse.

55
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,211
Yeah, well, D.C. asked.

56
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:52,546
You know, they want someone
outside of D.E.A.

57
00:02:53,297 --> 00:02:55,132
Look, I don't want this
to be awkward.

58
00:02:55,341 --> 00:02:56,384
Why?

59
00:02:56,842 --> 00:02:59,428
Because when you worked for me,
you were barely shaving?

60
00:03:00,429 --> 00:03:01,972
Yeah. Something like that.

61
00:03:02,932 --> 00:03:05,476
It's been a long time
since Rio Bravo station.

62
00:03:05,601 --> 00:03:06,977
You've come up in the world.

63
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:11,482
- Still, we did some good work.
- Yes, we did.

64
00:03:13,275 --> 00:03:15,361
So, look, I am gonna
need to talk to your people

65
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:17,822
- and take a look at the files.
- Have at it.

66
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:20,074
Alamo Brewhouse
was just bad luck.

67
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:22,868
And you didn't find
any drugs?

68
00:03:23,494 --> 00:03:25,162
Different day,
we would have.

69
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:28,749
I wanna start with the agent
who led the raid, Gonzalez.

70
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:32,670
You know, I understand that the restaurant
owner filed a complaint against him.

71
00:03:33,295 --> 00:03:36,424
Gonzo got a little overheated,
you know.

72
00:03:36,882 --> 00:03:38,300
He's on administrative leave.

73
00:03:38,551 --> 00:03:40,720
I'll... I'll get you
his home address.

74
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:46,684
Dennis, I'm gonna wanna take a look
at that report of yours before it goes in.

75
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,898
Well, you know,
that's not how we do things, Bill.

76
00:03:54,316 --> 00:03:55,526
A lot of people in this agency

77
00:03:55,651 --> 00:03:58,571
got their gunsights set
for ol' Bill Peterson.

78
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:01,574
I need to know if you're handing 'em
any bullets.

79
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:05,119
Well, I'm sorry.
My hands are tied.

80
00:04:06,328 --> 00:04:09,623
When I was your boss at Rio Bravo,
I had your back.

81
00:04:10,958 --> 00:04:12,918
You're telling me
you don't have mine now?

82
00:04:13,627 --> 00:04:14,795
Is that how you wanna play this?

83
00:04:16,005 --> 00:04:17,047
Come on.

84
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:19,425
I'm just looking for a little
professional courtesy.

85
00:04:24,346 --> 00:04:25,598
I'll see what I can do, Bill.

86
00:04:26,974 --> 00:04:28,017
All right.

87
00:04:28,934 --> 00:04:29,977
Thanks.

88
00:04:39,278 --> 00:04:41,697
"I don't understand why you have to
write the damn report."

89
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:42,948
Oh, it's nothing.

90
00:04:43,073 --> 00:04:46,035
I'll write it, D.C. will ignore it
and we'll get on with our lives.

91
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:47,870
- "How are you, baby?"
- Good.

92
00:04:48,204 --> 00:04:50,122
I just had lunch with a senator.
I'm meeting with the chair

93
00:04:50,247 --> 00:04:52,041
of the energy and commerce
committee in an hour.

94
00:04:52,416 --> 00:04:53,459
"It's exciting."

95
00:04:54,293 --> 00:04:55,336
I wish I were there.

96
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:57,254
- "I'll call you tonight, okay?"
- I love you.

97
00:04:58,005 --> 00:04:59,048
I love you, too.

98
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:42,883
FBI!
Agent Gonzalez, are you in here?

99
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:18,878
Abbott said it was the death
of a D.E.A. agent.

100
00:06:19,336 --> 00:06:21,046
By the way,
keep tomorrow night open.

101
00:06:21,171 --> 00:06:23,799
- Why would it be closed?
- Your birthday.

102
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:25,843
Oh, that. Yes.

103
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:29,555
I already told everybody at work...
no songs, no cake, no gifts.

104
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,223
- Good. Thank you.
- Except me.

105
00:06:31,348 --> 00:06:33,350
- Oh, you have a gift for me?
- It's a surprise.

106
00:06:33,517 --> 00:06:35,185
- A surprise?
- That's right.

107
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:39,273
You think you can keep a secret
from me for that long?

108
00:06:39,523 --> 00:06:41,859
I don't think I can. I know I can.

109
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:45,195
I admire your confidence.

110
00:06:55,287 --> 00:06:58,415
So, Vega, I've got tickets
to that Blues festival

111
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:00,500
and I was wondering...

112
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:02,836
Not "Vega." Michelle.

113
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:07,633
Michelle, I've got tickets,
and I was...

114
00:07:07,758 --> 00:07:09,009
Hey.

115
00:07:10,135 --> 00:07:11,178
Hi.

116
00:07:11,803 --> 00:07:13,555
{\an8}- You okay?
- Yeah.

117
00:07:14,473 --> 00:07:17,184
{\an8}- So Michelle...
- Abbott wants us. Caught a case.

118
00:07:17,351 --> 00:07:19,561
{\an8}O-Okay. Great.
Yeah, I'll be right there.

119
00:07:20,312 --> 00:07:21,355
{\an8}Okay.

120
00:07:25,442 --> 00:07:26,485
Good morning, everyone.

121
00:07:27,235 --> 00:07:29,905
{\an8}This is Bill Peterson,
San Antonio D.E.A.

122
00:07:30,530 --> 00:07:32,532
{\an8}Our victim's name
is Darrell Gonzalez.

123
00:07:32,699 --> 00:07:34,451
He's been with the D.E.A.
for seven years.

124
00:07:34,576 --> 00:07:36,244
Served in Afghanistan
before that.

125
00:07:38,038 --> 00:07:40,666
I want you all to know how much
I appreciate your help.

126
00:07:43,669 --> 00:07:45,629
{\an8}We're gonna get the pigs
who did this.

127
00:07:47,714 --> 00:07:50,384
{\an8}We understand how hard it is
to lose somebody.

128
00:07:51,343 --> 00:07:53,136
{\an8}We will extend every courtesy
to you.

129
00:07:54,763 --> 00:07:55,889
{\an8}Every courtesy?

130
00:07:56,682 --> 00:07:58,058
{\an8}That's the Sosa cartel tag.

131
00:07:58,183 --> 00:07:59,601
Looks like they're trying
to send a message.

132
00:07:59,977 --> 00:08:02,938
{\an8}Gonzo had just led a raid
on a restaurant

133
00:08:03,063 --> 00:08:05,524
{\an8}that was distributing
Sosa narcotics.

134
00:08:06,191 --> 00:08:07,567
{\an8}And it was owned
by this man.

135
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,403
Steven Korbell.

136
00:08:09,695 --> 00:08:11,989
How does a restaurant owner
become a drug dealer?

137
00:08:12,447 --> 00:08:14,992
{\an8}He used to manage a hotel
in Mexico City

138
00:08:15,158 --> 00:08:16,284
{\an8}that was owned
by the Sosas.

139
00:08:16,410 --> 00:08:18,161
{\an8}That's when he began working
with them.

140
00:08:18,286 --> 00:08:21,206
{\an8}In the raid that Gonzalez led,
they didn't find anything.

141
00:08:21,331 --> 00:08:24,835
{\an8}Why would Korbell order a hit
after an unsuccessful raid?

142
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,378
{\an8}I mean, it just calls
more attention to him.

143
00:08:26,545 --> 00:08:27,587
{\an8}Exactly.

144
00:08:27,713 --> 00:08:31,550
{\an8}The animal that escapes a snare doesn't
necessarily go after the poacher.

145
00:08:31,675 --> 00:08:34,636
{\an8}Okay, everyone, we can ask
these questions in San Antonio.

146
00:08:34,845 --> 00:08:36,054
So, saddle up.

147
00:08:47,190 --> 00:08:49,026
What does this guy Peterson
have on you?

148
00:08:49,568 --> 00:08:50,610
{\an8}Why do you ask?

149
00:08:50,944 --> 00:08:53,196
{\an8}Because you're acting like
he has something on you.

150
00:08:54,573 --> 00:08:55,615
He doesn't.

151
00:08:57,325 --> 00:08:58,368
{\an8}Okay.

152
00:09:09,421 --> 00:09:11,965
- Gonzalez's desk?
- Yeah, we were neighbors.

153
00:09:12,507 --> 00:09:14,551
Man, he used to listen
to the worst music.

154
00:09:14,676 --> 00:09:16,219
{\an8}Smooth jazz.

155
00:09:17,095 --> 00:09:19,556
{\an8}Let's see.
Alamo Brewhouse file.

156
00:09:19,723 --> 00:09:21,224
{\an8}- Yeah.
- That's thorough.

157
00:09:21,349 --> 00:09:22,726
Yeah, he didn't talk computers.

158
00:09:22,851 --> 00:09:24,686
He kept a hard copy
on everything...

159
00:09:25,312 --> 00:09:26,396
financial records

160
00:09:26,521 --> 00:09:28,648
witness interviews,
surveillance photos.

161
00:09:29,316 --> 00:09:30,984
My kind of people.
You mind if I take a look?

162
00:09:31,318 --> 00:09:32,736
{\an8}- Dig in.
- Thank you.

163
00:09:38,784 --> 00:09:39,951
{\an8}How long had Agent Gonzalez

164
00:09:40,077 --> 00:09:41,787
{\an8}been investigating
the Alamo Brewhouse?

165
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:45,165
- Months.
- Gonzo was relentless.

166
00:09:45,624 --> 00:09:47,542
He slept here on the couch
half the week.

167
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:50,712
Agent Bordick, you were
the analyst working with him?

168
00:09:50,962 --> 00:09:52,005
What are you implying?

169
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:55,217
I'm implying you were
the analyst working with him.

170
00:09:55,550 --> 00:09:56,718
We had this one right.

171
00:09:57,677 --> 00:09:58,970
That restaurant was a front

172
00:09:59,179 --> 00:10:01,848
and we must've just missed
the supply re-up.

173
00:10:02,182 --> 00:10:03,809
This wasn't your
first time coming up empty.

174
00:10:04,017 --> 00:10:05,268
Your team's had other misses.

175
00:10:05,435 --> 00:10:07,521
How long have the two of you
been out of the Academy?

176
00:10:08,522 --> 00:10:09,898
- An hour?
- Whoa.

177
00:10:10,023 --> 00:10:12,317
- Easy, Jeff.
- It's okay, Agent Orosco.

178
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:15,445
We'd be happy to send you
our CVs if you like.

179
00:10:31,861 --> 00:10:33,654
Did you have any contact
with Gonzalez

180
00:10:33,779 --> 00:10:36,699
in the days following the raid,
after he was on leave?

181
00:10:36,907 --> 00:10:38,743
No. No, but that wasn't unusual.

182
00:10:38,909 --> 00:10:39,952
Do you know what he was doing?

183
00:10:40,536 --> 00:10:42,163
Knowing Gonzo,
he was probably obsessing

184
00:10:42,288 --> 00:10:43,456
over why that raid went south.

185
00:10:43,748 --> 00:10:45,875
Excuse me. That's the front
of the restaurant, right?

186
00:10:46,042 --> 00:10:47,835
Yeah. Those are
the surveillance photos.

187
00:10:48,252 --> 00:10:49,295
Taken over a few days?

188
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:51,630
- No, we staked it out for a few weeks.
- Excellent.

189
00:10:51,756 --> 00:10:53,591
You know where the owner
of the restaurant is?

190
00:10:53,758 --> 00:10:56,844
He's here. He's talking to Cho
and one of the D.E.A. agents.

191
00:10:59,889 --> 00:11:00,931
What's he doing?

192
00:11:01,432 --> 00:11:03,392
Mr. Korbell is a community pillar.

193
00:11:03,642 --> 00:11:06,395
He sponsors chili cook-offs
and youth baseball teams.

194
00:11:06,687 --> 00:11:07,730
He's not a killer.

195
00:11:07,855 --> 00:11:09,815
He's got a hell of a P.R. Department,
I'll give him that.

196
00:11:10,024 --> 00:11:12,276
Where were you yesterday
from 8:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m.?

197
00:11:12,985 --> 00:11:15,279
In Dallas. I had business.

198
00:11:16,155 --> 00:11:17,865
Produce evidence of a crime,
gentlemen.

199
00:11:18,324 --> 00:11:20,159
So far you've done a bang-up job
of the opposite.

200
00:11:21,619 --> 00:11:24,580
- Hi. Patrick Jane. FBI.
- What the hell is this?

201
00:11:24,705 --> 00:11:26,123
- Hey, Cho.
- Hi, Jane.

202
00:11:27,124 --> 00:11:28,709
- Korbell?
- Yeah.

203
00:11:29,043 --> 00:11:31,545
Very important question.
What time does your restaurant open?

204
00:11:34,882 --> 00:11:35,925
Noon.

205
00:11:36,217 --> 00:11:38,260
So you'll be opening
in a little under an hour.

206
00:11:38,469 --> 00:11:39,970
If I'm not wasting
my time here, yeah.

207
00:11:41,430 --> 00:11:42,681
- These two are free to go.
- Hey!

208
00:11:42,807 --> 00:11:44,475
Have a lovely afternoon.
Thanks for your time.

209
00:11:45,559 --> 00:11:48,646
- You can't do this, man.
- Yes, he can. You can go.

210
00:12:00,950 --> 00:12:01,992
Hey.

211
00:12:03,202 --> 00:12:05,162
- What the hell is this, man?
- Easy, tiger.

212
00:12:05,287 --> 00:12:08,374
FBI is sending a team in to raid
that restaurant this afternoon.

213
00:12:08,499 --> 00:12:10,543
If we find drugs, we wanna make sure
Korbell's there.

214
00:12:11,043 --> 00:12:14,296
- Why didn't anybody tell us?
- What did I just do?

215
00:12:22,012 --> 00:12:23,055
Hey.

216
00:12:24,014 --> 00:12:25,808
You're never gonna believe
what this guy just told me.

217
00:12:55,546 --> 00:12:57,423
Care to tell me
why we're here?

218
00:12:57,673 --> 00:12:58,716
Of course.

219
00:12:58,841 --> 00:13:00,384
In three minutes.

220
00:13:01,343 --> 00:13:04,346
- How do you know Peterson?
- I worked for him.

221
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:05,723
A long time ago.

222
00:13:06,599 --> 00:13:09,852
- You must've been very green.
- Oh, you have no idea.

223
00:13:11,061 --> 00:13:12,104
Agent Peterson.

224
00:13:13,522 --> 00:13:14,690
Were your ears burning?

225
00:13:16,567 --> 00:13:17,735
Dennis. What's up?

226
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:20,779
- You're raiding Alamo Brewhouse?
- No.

227
00:13:20,946 --> 00:13:24,533
This one here told my people
you're sending in a strike team.

228
00:13:25,159 --> 00:13:26,452
I did. Sorry.

229
00:13:26,952 --> 00:13:28,871
- That was a lie.
- What?

230
00:13:29,079 --> 00:13:30,581
A fib. An untruth.

231
00:13:31,207 --> 00:13:32,249
I made it up.

232
00:13:32,625 --> 00:13:33,876
Have a seat. I'll explain.

233
00:13:38,631 --> 00:13:41,508
Do either of you notice the difference
from this photo to this photo?

234
00:13:42,843 --> 00:13:43,886
Where's Waldo?

235
00:13:44,094 --> 00:13:45,512
There's a light bulb on the sign

236
00:13:45,638 --> 00:13:48,140
that's off in one photo
and on in the other.

237
00:13:48,265 --> 00:13:50,100
So they had
a broken light bulb.

238
00:13:50,851 --> 00:13:54,313
But then it's on again here...
And off...

239
00:13:55,105 --> 00:13:56,148
And on.

240
00:13:57,733 --> 00:13:58,776
It's a signal.

241
00:13:59,610 --> 00:14:01,487
When the light is on,
they're selling drugs.

242
00:14:01,779 --> 00:14:03,781
When it's off, they're not.

243
00:14:04,031 --> 00:14:05,658
This photo was taken the day
of your raid.

244
00:14:05,783 --> 00:14:07,326
You notice how the light is off?

245
00:14:07,576 --> 00:14:09,245
And that's why you guys
didn't find anything.

246
00:14:10,246 --> 00:14:11,288
They weren't selling.

247
00:14:11,413 --> 00:14:12,665
But why that day, huh?

248
00:14:13,791 --> 00:14:14,833
Was it just bad luck?

249
00:14:16,502 --> 00:14:19,171
Here we are.
12:00 on the dot.

250
00:14:24,468 --> 00:14:25,511
Oh no.

251
00:14:26,345 --> 00:14:28,347
The green light is on today.

252
00:14:29,056 --> 00:14:30,099
I turned it on.

253
00:14:30,516 --> 00:14:31,976
But what do you think
Korbell is gonna do

254
00:14:32,101 --> 00:14:34,103
when he thinks
another raid is coming?

255
00:14:38,774 --> 00:14:39,817
"And here you go."

256
00:14:40,651 --> 00:14:41,694
Wait a minute.

257
00:14:42,695 --> 00:14:46,323
- How could Korbell know that?
- He has an inside source.

258
00:14:46,615 --> 00:14:47,825
Someone from D.E.A.

259
00:14:47,950 --> 00:14:50,869
And if I figured it out,
Gonzalez did.

260
00:14:51,829 --> 00:14:52,955
That's what got him killed.

261
00:14:53,831 --> 00:14:55,124
What are you saying?

262
00:14:55,666 --> 00:14:59,169
That someone on your team
is a killer.

263
00:15:08,610 --> 00:15:10,946
So, we're looking for a cop
that killed a cop.

264
00:15:11,446 --> 00:15:12,781
Gonzalez must have figured out
there was a mole.

265
00:15:12,906 --> 00:15:14,366
The mole killed him
before he could go public.

266
00:15:14,491 --> 00:15:16,284
Whoever it is,
he's been at it a while.

267
00:15:16,451 --> 00:15:19,621
There have been a half a dozen
busted raids in the past two years.

268
00:15:19,746 --> 00:15:23,542
Peterson's explained them all away...
bad Intel, tactical mistakes.

269
00:15:23,834 --> 00:15:25,752
In hindsight, it had to have
been an inside man.

270
00:15:25,919 --> 00:15:28,255
So for now
we don't rule out anyone.

271
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:30,340
It could be any one
of Peterson's agents.

272
00:15:30,465 --> 00:15:33,593
- That's 30 suspects.
- 31. You forgot Peterson.

273
00:15:34,136 --> 00:15:36,263
Bill Peterson doesn't have
much of a bedside manner

274
00:15:36,388 --> 00:15:37,597
but he's not a traitor.

275
00:15:37,848 --> 00:15:39,224
I thought we couldn't
rule anyone out.

276
00:15:40,267 --> 00:15:42,310
Abbott's right.
Peterson's not a suspect.

277
00:15:43,728 --> 00:15:47,649
Good. So, we'll,
just dig down into his team.

278
00:15:47,816 --> 00:15:50,986
Personal reviews, bank records.
Anything that points to a motive.

279
00:15:51,111 --> 00:15:53,989
Ego, revenge.
What? You disagree?

280
00:15:55,282 --> 00:15:58,160
Well, they're all poorly paid
government employees.

281
00:15:58,285 --> 00:16:00,662
You're not gonna have to dig
too deep to find motive.

282
00:16:01,371 --> 00:16:03,582
- You have a better idea?
- Maybe.

283
00:16:04,207 --> 00:16:07,252
But first, I need someone
to run an errand for me.

284
00:16:11,339 --> 00:16:12,382
Back at the D.E.A.

285
00:16:12,507 --> 00:16:14,342
what were you and Orosco
saying to each other?

286
00:16:14,509 --> 00:16:16,720
Oh, he was apologizing
for his partner being a jerk.

287
00:16:17,012 --> 00:16:18,054
I said it was fine.

288
00:16:19,014 --> 00:16:20,182
"You don't speak Spanish?"

289
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:22,559
I speak at a ninth-grade level.

290
00:16:23,059 --> 00:16:25,270
I can say "grandmother"
and "hall pass."

291
00:16:26,313 --> 00:16:29,149
- Do you speak any other languages?
- I'm fluent in pig Latin.

292
00:16:30,233 --> 00:16:32,611
- I'm not really sure that counts.
- Listen, I wanted...

293
00:16:32,736 --> 00:16:35,572
Vega, I need you to do something.
But first, a question.

294
00:16:35,989 --> 00:16:38,450
Uh, we shoot new pictures
for the I.D. badges every year.

295
00:16:38,575 --> 00:16:39,993
Does every federal agency do that?

296
00:16:40,118 --> 00:16:41,745
- I think so.
- Excellent.

297
00:16:41,953 --> 00:16:43,872
I need you to go back
to San Antonio.

298
00:16:43,997 --> 00:16:46,917
I need you to get all photo I.D.s
for Peterson's D.E.A. team

299
00:16:47,042 --> 00:16:48,084
for the past three years.

300
00:16:48,210 --> 00:16:49,794
We just got back
from San Antonio.

301
00:16:50,003 --> 00:16:52,506
I know. No rest for the weary
crimefighter.

302
00:16:54,049 --> 00:16:55,842
- See you when I get back.
- Yeah.

303
00:17:04,935 --> 00:17:06,520
- Abbott.
- "Dennis."

304
00:17:06,770 --> 00:17:09,189
I'm in Austin. Like to talk,
if you got a minute.

305
00:17:10,106 --> 00:17:11,483
Sure. Come by the office.

306
00:17:11,775 --> 00:17:14,402
Actually, I'd prefer talking
outside your office.

307
00:17:14,861 --> 00:17:16,530
"Mind meeting me
at Graham Plaza?"

308
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:22,953
Evening, Bill.

309
00:17:24,037 --> 00:17:25,080
You want a drink?

310
00:17:25,789 --> 00:17:27,582
- Club soda. Thanks.
- Another one.

311
00:17:30,627 --> 00:17:32,420
A hell of a thing to know

312
00:17:32,546 --> 00:17:35,131
that one of your people
betrayed you.

313
00:17:35,715 --> 00:17:38,009
Killed a colleague.
A friend.

314
00:17:38,260 --> 00:17:39,386
Yeah, it's hard, I know.

315
00:17:39,970 --> 00:17:41,388
You didn't tell
your team anything?

316
00:17:41,805 --> 00:17:45,684
No. They think it's an investigation
of a cartel murder.

317
00:17:46,017 --> 00:17:47,686
Well, my people
are the best, Bill.

318
00:17:48,728 --> 00:17:49,771
We'll get this guy.

319
00:17:50,939 --> 00:17:51,982
I'm sure you will.

320
00:17:52,983 --> 00:17:55,986
When you do,
I need to share the collar.

321
00:17:56,653 --> 00:17:59,990
- What do you mean?
- I want credit for the arrest.

322
00:18:00,574 --> 00:18:01,908
We'll come up
with something I did...

323
00:18:02,033 --> 00:18:05,579
something vital to the
investigation, you know.

324
00:18:05,745 --> 00:18:07,038
So you want me
to lie for you.

325
00:18:07,872 --> 00:18:09,165
I told you, I have enemies.

326
00:18:09,291 --> 00:18:12,043
They find out one of my people
was working for the cartel

327
00:18:12,627 --> 00:18:14,671
they'll take me to town
unless I do something.

328
00:18:14,796 --> 00:18:16,423
I need to be part
of the solution.

329
00:18:16,590 --> 00:18:18,466
You have been asleep
at the wheel.

330
00:18:19,384 --> 00:18:20,760
One of your people
has been in bed

331
00:18:20,885 --> 00:18:23,263
with the Sosas for two years,
and you didn't see it.

332
00:18:23,847 --> 00:18:25,432
Now you want me
to cover your ass?

333
00:18:25,557 --> 00:18:28,184
We should be having a discussion
about your resignation.

334
00:18:30,687 --> 00:18:33,189
We've all done things
we're not proud of, Dennis...

335
00:18:33,690 --> 00:18:35,358
things we'd like
kept quiet.

336
00:18:42,115 --> 00:18:44,492
So you're gonna hang Rio Bravo
over my head

337
00:18:44,743 --> 00:18:45,869
unless I play along.

338
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:48,622
I wish it was just you.

339
00:18:49,998 --> 00:18:53,918
Lena's confirmation is coming up
in a couple of weeks, right?

340
00:18:54,919 --> 00:18:58,757
Rio Bravo could be
a real problem there, too.

341
00:19:06,264 --> 00:19:08,058
I need this, Dennis.

342
00:19:10,518 --> 00:19:11,561
Keep me posted.

343
00:19:29,037 --> 00:19:30,163
You ready to get out of here?

344
00:19:31,498 --> 00:19:33,917
- I think I'm gonna stick around.
- Okay.

345
00:19:34,793 --> 00:19:37,003
Any guesses about your present?
Or have you given up?

346
00:19:37,337 --> 00:19:39,798
Does it weigh more or less
than 3 1/2 pounds?

347
00:19:40,882 --> 00:19:42,217
Why 3 1/2 pounds?

348
00:19:42,342 --> 00:19:43,885
- Because.
- Less.

349
00:19:44,010 --> 00:19:45,762
- Is it made of Kryptonite?
- No.

350
00:19:46,096 --> 00:19:48,932
Is it something that I would
wear on a cold winter's day?

351
00:19:49,099 --> 00:19:50,141
No.

352
00:19:56,314 --> 00:19:59,150
That is my guess.

353
00:19:59,401 --> 00:20:02,153
Promise me you will not open it
till tomorrow night.

354
00:20:02,278 --> 00:20:04,239
- You are so bluffing. Aren't you?
- See you later.

355
00:20:18,670 --> 00:20:22,132
I'm guessing by your look
that you just talked to Peterson.

356
00:20:24,551 --> 00:20:25,593
I'm listening.

357
00:20:30,515 --> 00:20:32,392
I worked for him
about ten years ago

358
00:20:33,351 --> 00:20:35,770
when he was running a task force
on the border.

359
00:20:36,813 --> 00:20:38,106
Rio Bravo station.

360
00:20:40,442 --> 00:20:42,026
We were working
with the Mexican police

361
00:20:42,152 --> 00:20:44,362
trying to do something
about the cartels.

362
00:20:44,779 --> 00:20:46,990
- Tough work.
- It was war.

363
00:20:51,119 --> 00:20:54,330
The Zeta cartel would send their
men out dressed like soldiers.

364
00:20:55,248 --> 00:20:57,041
They would wait for a bus
to come through

365
00:20:57,751 --> 00:21:00,962
stop it, force all
the passengers off

366
00:21:02,130 --> 00:21:03,173
and shoot them.

367
00:21:04,257 --> 00:21:05,300
All of them.

368
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:09,345
Just so they didn't work
for another cartel.

369
00:21:10,722 --> 00:21:12,682
There were bodies everywhere.

370
00:21:13,224 --> 00:21:16,394
Men, women, children...

371
00:21:17,604 --> 00:21:20,023
Scattered all over the road
like trash.

372
00:21:21,107 --> 00:21:25,570
Yeah, it's... it's no picture
that anyone should have in their head.

373
00:21:28,031 --> 00:21:32,160
One day I was sitting
on a Zeta safe house...

374
00:21:32,285 --> 00:21:35,497
just watching
who came and went.

375
00:21:37,665 --> 00:21:38,708
Gathering Intel.

376
00:21:41,878 --> 00:21:42,921
And I saw this...

377
00:21:44,923 --> 00:21:48,635
- Zeta commander walk out.
- Dressed in a military uniform.

378
00:21:49,761 --> 00:21:51,930
And I knew what he was gonna do.

379
00:21:54,349 --> 00:21:57,477
I couldn't call the local police
because they were terrified of the Zetas.

380
00:21:58,853 --> 00:21:59,896
I couldn't arrest him.

381
00:22:01,815 --> 00:22:05,693
So I sat there, thinking...
I don't know...

382
00:22:05,819 --> 00:22:07,946
maybe three seconds.

383
00:22:10,990 --> 00:22:12,033
I got out of my car

384
00:22:12,158 --> 00:22:15,078
I walked across the street,
and I shot him.

385
00:22:22,961 --> 00:22:24,003
You...

386
00:22:25,588 --> 00:22:26,714
You did the right thing.

387
00:22:30,468 --> 00:22:31,511
I don't know.

388
00:22:33,721 --> 00:22:35,431
But no buses were stopped that night.

389
00:22:37,392 --> 00:22:39,978
And the next day
I quit the Rio Bravo station.

390
00:22:41,354 --> 00:22:42,856
Did Peterson know
what you had done?

391
00:22:44,607 --> 00:22:45,650
He guessed.

392
00:22:47,902 --> 00:22:51,155
The death of a commander
hit the news.

393
00:22:51,406 --> 00:22:53,908
Tons of speculation
on who killed him and...

394
00:22:54,868 --> 00:22:57,120
Peterson knew
where I was when it happened.

395
00:22:57,954 --> 00:23:00,164
And now he's threatening you
to do what he says.

396
00:23:00,415 --> 00:23:03,167
Peterson can end my career.
I can go to prison.

397
00:23:05,336 --> 00:23:07,547
But it's not just about me.

398
00:23:07,881 --> 00:23:12,594
Any mention of this could end things
for Lena before it even starts.

399
00:23:13,636 --> 00:23:15,013
Well, you can't let him do it.

400
00:23:16,347 --> 00:23:17,849
I appreciate the thought.

401
00:23:20,852 --> 00:23:22,186
How do we stop him?

402
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:26,482
I'm not sure.

403
00:23:28,401 --> 00:23:29,444
Yet.

404
00:23:32,530 --> 00:23:34,616
But when I know,
I'll tell you the answer.

405
00:23:53,941 --> 00:23:56,193
- Hey, can you help me with something?
- Sure.

406
00:23:57,403 --> 00:23:59,113
Abbott asked me to look
into Korbell's records

407
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:02,074
see how he's communicating
with his contact on Peterson's team.

408
00:24:02,283 --> 00:24:05,494
I've looked at Korbell's
phone, e-mails, texts.

409
00:24:05,870 --> 00:24:06,912
Nothing jumps out.

410
00:24:07,038 --> 00:24:09,040
They're too smart to use
something that easy to get into.

411
00:24:09,248 --> 00:24:10,624
They must have been making
contact somehow.

412
00:24:10,750 --> 00:24:11,792
Check his day-to-day.

413
00:24:11,917 --> 00:24:13,294
What was Korbell looking
at on the web?

414
00:24:14,295 --> 00:24:17,798
Based on the sites he visits
he's a Houston fan.

415
00:24:17,923 --> 00:24:21,969
He buys a lot of protein powder.
He's into Persian longhairs.

416
00:24:22,470 --> 00:24:23,512
The cats?

417
00:24:23,929 --> 00:24:25,389
- Yeah.
- No way.

418
00:24:25,973 --> 00:24:28,726
Way. He spends a lot of time
on a Persian longhair website.

419
00:24:28,851 --> 00:24:31,687
I've read his file.
There is no way Korbell is into cats.

420
00:24:31,812 --> 00:24:34,273
He's too macho
too desperate for approval.

421
00:24:34,398 --> 00:24:35,649
Must have been going there
for something.

422
00:24:35,775 --> 00:24:37,401
Maybe they're communicating
through the message boards.

423
00:24:37,526 --> 00:24:38,819
Nobody would look
there first.

424
00:24:39,070 --> 00:24:40,112
I'll check it out.

425
00:24:43,365 --> 00:24:45,117
- I got the I.D. pictures.
- Thank you.

426
00:24:45,284 --> 00:24:47,912
The past three years for each person
on Peterson's team.

427
00:24:48,079 --> 00:24:49,872
30 in total.
Most recent pictures on top.

428
00:24:49,997 --> 00:24:51,582
You're a marvel, Vega.
Well done.

429
00:25:08,808 --> 00:25:09,850
What are you looking at?

430
00:25:10,601 --> 00:25:11,644
Their eyes.

431
00:25:12,019 --> 00:25:14,855
- Windows to the soul.
- You can't be serious.

432
00:25:15,189 --> 00:25:16,482
Good call, Vega.

433
00:25:16,857 --> 00:25:18,317
Really, what are you looking at?

434
00:25:18,484 --> 00:25:20,778
Well, I don't wanna ruin the surprise
but since you're interested

435
00:25:20,903 --> 00:25:22,655
there may be something
you can help me with.

436
00:25:23,405 --> 00:25:26,575
Requires some bravado
which should be right up your alley.

437
00:25:26,992 --> 00:25:30,037
- Help you with what?
- A little something to catch a killer.

438
00:25:31,705 --> 00:25:35,126
- You want me to help you with a trick.
- Well, if that's what you wanna call it.

439
00:25:35,876 --> 00:25:36,919
Problem?

440
00:25:38,879 --> 00:25:40,172
Speak your mind, soldier.

441
00:25:42,716 --> 00:25:43,759
It's just...

442
00:25:45,511 --> 00:25:48,472
I very much appreciate being
a part of this team, sir.

443
00:25:49,056 --> 00:25:50,099
You get results.

444
00:25:50,224 --> 00:25:52,059
- I respect that.
- Thank you. But?

445
00:25:54,895 --> 00:25:56,480
The things you ask people
to do...

446
00:25:57,857 --> 00:25:58,899
it's...

447
00:25:59,567 --> 00:26:02,319
It's not what I thought working
for the FBI would be like.

448
00:26:02,820 --> 00:26:04,238
- At all.
- No.

449
00:26:04,405 --> 00:26:07,741
And, uh, more importantly

450
00:26:08,075 --> 00:26:09,952
you wonder if your father
would approve.

451
00:26:12,538 --> 00:26:13,581
Sometimes.

452
00:26:15,249 --> 00:26:16,333
He was strict.

453
00:26:17,168 --> 00:26:20,296
37 years in the military
makes you a stickler for the rules.

454
00:26:20,504 --> 00:26:21,672
I'm sure he was.

455
00:26:22,590 --> 00:26:25,134
And a good father.
And you're proof of that.

456
00:26:26,260 --> 00:26:29,013
But I can't tell you what your father
would approve of.

457
00:26:32,224 --> 00:26:33,434
That's for you to decide.

458
00:26:39,273 --> 00:26:41,233
- Sir?
- Yes, Vega?

459
00:26:43,569 --> 00:26:44,695
What do you want me to do?

460
00:26:45,779 --> 00:26:48,616
Well, when I'm finished here,
I'll tell you.

461
00:26:50,659 --> 00:26:51,702
Sure.

462
00:26:53,787 --> 00:26:54,830
Thank you.

463
00:27:04,381 --> 00:27:06,884
- Abbott.
- Dennis, any progress?

464
00:27:08,677 --> 00:27:10,888
- Some.
- Don't make me chase you down.

465
00:27:11,013 --> 00:27:12,056
What's going on?

466
00:27:13,724 --> 00:27:15,059
We're gathering information.

467
00:27:15,476 --> 00:27:17,269
"Let me know as soon
as you got something."

468
00:27:17,770 --> 00:27:19,021
"Don't hold out on me."

469
00:27:19,647 --> 00:27:21,023
That will not go well.

470
00:27:32,368 --> 00:27:34,245
- Making progress?
- Yes, actually.

471
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:37,915
Got something. Korbell was trading
messages with his contact

472
00:27:38,040 --> 00:27:39,750
on Peterson's team
through a cat blog.

473
00:27:40,251 --> 00:27:41,293
What was in the messages?

474
00:27:41,418 --> 00:27:43,754
Coded language
about D.E.A. investigations.

475
00:27:43,879 --> 00:27:45,756
The first letter of each word
spells the message.

476
00:27:45,881 --> 00:27:47,258
So, for instance...

477
00:27:47,675 --> 00:27:49,885
"Reactive allergies
in de-clawed animals?"

478
00:27:50,010 --> 00:27:53,889
"Try 4 preventative measures."
That spells "Raid at 4pm."

479
00:27:54,848 --> 00:27:55,933
It's actually pretty cool.

480
00:27:56,183 --> 00:27:58,018
- Do we know who Korbell was dealing with?
- No.

481
00:27:58,143 --> 00:28:00,896
Whoever it is has covered his tracks
with proxy servers and VPNs.

482
00:28:01,063 --> 00:28:03,065
- Whatever they are.
- But here's something interesting.

483
00:28:03,190 --> 00:28:05,901
As of yesterday,
he suddenly stopped posting.

484
00:28:06,610 --> 00:28:07,695
There are no new messages.

485
00:28:08,779 --> 00:28:11,198
- He's getting ready to run.
- Maybe he's just laying low.

486
00:28:11,490 --> 00:28:14,326
Well, a poker player that stops betting
isn't laying low.

487
00:28:14,451 --> 00:28:15,494
He's cashing in.

488
00:28:15,619 --> 00:28:17,579
Well, if he's about to rabbit,
then we better move quickly.

489
00:28:17,705 --> 00:28:19,748
It's perfect.
Call San Antonio.

490
00:28:19,873 --> 00:28:21,292
Tell them there's been
a breakthrough in the case.

491
00:28:21,625 --> 00:28:25,838
Have them gather up these ten agents
and I'll go talk to them in two hours.

492
00:28:38,267 --> 00:28:39,310
Everybody's here.

493
00:28:40,686 --> 00:28:41,812
You needn't worry.

494
00:28:42,604 --> 00:28:44,690
- I'm not worried.
- Good.

495
00:28:47,568 --> 00:28:48,652
Vega, you're on.

496
00:28:49,236 --> 00:28:50,738
"Just stay relaxed.
You'll be just fine."

497
00:28:51,864 --> 00:28:52,906
Thank you, sir.

498
00:28:58,078 --> 00:28:59,121
Let's go.

499
00:29:05,794 --> 00:29:06,837
Agent Peterson.

500
00:29:08,255 --> 00:29:10,049
You're one of Abbott's people, right?

501
00:29:11,050 --> 00:29:13,427
I'll be down to whatever
he's doing in a minute.

502
00:29:15,137 --> 00:29:16,638
Actually, sir...

503
00:29:18,015 --> 00:29:19,058
You're under arrest.

504
00:29:22,478 --> 00:29:23,562
I'm what?

505
00:29:24,521 --> 00:29:25,564
Thank you for coming.

506
00:29:25,689 --> 00:29:27,649
Could you all take a seat
up front here, please?

507
00:29:28,067 --> 00:29:29,109
Thank you.

508
00:29:33,781 --> 00:29:35,157
I know you're wondering
why you're here.

509
00:29:35,324 --> 00:29:36,784
The answer to that is simple...

510
00:29:37,993 --> 00:29:40,079
one of you killed
Darrell Gonzalez.

511
00:29:40,579 --> 00:29:42,039
- And...
- What?

512
00:29:42,164 --> 00:29:44,750
I'm gonna tell you who
in about five minutes.

513
00:29:44,875 --> 00:29:47,252
Agents Cho and Lisbon
will come through the aisles.

514
00:29:47,461 --> 00:29:49,254
We're asking you
to give up your guns.

515
00:29:49,922 --> 00:29:50,964
You got to be kidding me.

516
00:29:51,090 --> 00:29:52,383
We'll return the weapons
when this is over.

517
00:29:52,591 --> 00:29:54,218
If you're innocent,
there's no problem.

518
00:29:54,760 --> 00:29:57,513
If there's a killer in the room
we don't wanna risk a gun fight.

519
00:29:57,638 --> 00:29:59,264
We don't want anyone to get hurt.

520
00:29:59,556 --> 00:30:00,766
I'm afraid I have to insist.

521
00:30:00,891 --> 00:30:03,435
One of you is working
with the Sosa cartel

522
00:30:03,977 --> 00:30:05,020
and betrayed your team.

523
00:30:05,145 --> 00:30:07,898
If you're not interested
in knowing who that person is

524
00:30:08,023 --> 00:30:09,566
by all means, keep your guns.

525
00:30:24,790 --> 00:30:25,833
Thank you.

526
00:30:42,182 --> 00:30:43,225
Question...

527
00:30:44,435 --> 00:30:46,603
have any of you
recently inherited

528
00:30:46,728 --> 00:30:49,440
some money from a deceased
parent or grandparent?

529
00:30:49,898 --> 00:30:51,358
I'm not talking
about a little bit.

530
00:30:51,483 --> 00:30:53,026
A pile, enough to make a difference.

531
00:30:53,193 --> 00:30:54,361
Raise your hands, please.

532
00:30:54,945 --> 00:30:55,988
Don't be shy.

533
00:30:57,239 --> 00:30:59,825
I'm very sorry for your losses.

534
00:31:00,826 --> 00:31:02,744
None of you killed
Darrell Gonzalez.

535
00:31:02,870 --> 00:31:04,788
You can move to the back
of the room, please.

536
00:31:05,456 --> 00:31:06,498
Thank you.

537
00:31:06,999 --> 00:31:10,043
What does an inheritance
have to do with who killed Gonzalez?

538
00:31:10,210 --> 00:31:11,295
That is a good question.

539
00:31:11,503 --> 00:31:13,464
But I am the one
asking those right now.

540
00:31:13,797 --> 00:31:18,177
Now, is there anyone here in a relationship
with someone from the beauty field?

541
00:31:19,094 --> 00:31:23,348
Yeah. My husband runs a couple
of styling salons.

542
00:31:23,474 --> 00:31:24,600
How long have you been together?

543
00:31:25,934 --> 00:31:27,603
- A year.
- Congratulations.

544
00:31:27,728 --> 00:31:28,812
I'm very happy for you.

545
00:31:29,897 --> 00:31:31,190
You didn't kill Darrell Gonzalez.

546
00:31:31,315 --> 00:31:32,983
Would you move to the back
of the room, please?

547
00:31:34,067 --> 00:31:38,822
Anyone here get divorced
in the past three years?

548
00:31:40,574 --> 00:31:42,493
Yes, law enforcement...
tough on the home life.

549
00:31:42,826 --> 00:31:44,536
On the plus side,
you didn't kill Gonzalez.

550
00:31:44,661 --> 00:31:46,914
- Back you go, please.
- Oh. Wow.

551
00:31:47,039 --> 00:31:48,957
You think one of us are in bed
with the Sosas?

552
00:31:49,291 --> 00:31:51,793
- That's crazy.
- Really. Why would we do that?

553
00:31:52,127 --> 00:31:54,588
Money, I assume.
But I, I don't care about the motive.

554
00:31:54,963 --> 00:31:58,759
I'm interested in what happened
after one of you became a traitor.

555
00:31:59,927 --> 00:32:02,387
I looked at your I.D. pictures
for the last few years.

556
00:32:02,721 --> 00:32:04,848
All ten of you have improved
your appearance

557
00:32:05,265 --> 00:32:07,559
most noticeably by sprucing up
your hair.

558
00:32:07,726 --> 00:32:09,561
Some of you because
you inherited money

559
00:32:09,770 --> 00:32:12,022
others because you're back
in the dating scene.

560
00:32:12,356 --> 00:32:14,566
Are you seriously saying
that one of us is the killer

561
00:32:15,817 --> 00:32:17,069
because we got
a better haircut?

562
00:32:17,194 --> 00:32:20,239
A killer, no. A traitor, yes.

563
00:32:20,989 --> 00:32:25,953
Whoever sold out to the Sosas made bank
and got a big ego boost.

564
00:32:26,370 --> 00:32:29,456
When you have a good secret,
it makes you feel important.

565
00:32:30,624 --> 00:32:32,334
If you're so sure,
which one of us is it?

566
00:32:33,877 --> 00:32:36,380
- Well, that's the question, isn't it?
- Jane.

567
00:32:37,548 --> 00:32:39,508
- Just a minute, Vega.
- I found the killer.

568
00:32:42,344 --> 00:32:43,387
It's Bill Peterson.

569
00:32:55,028 --> 00:32:56,697
You're seriously doing this.

570
00:32:57,431 --> 00:32:59,391
I was certain it was gonna be
one of the other three agents.

571
00:32:59,516 --> 00:33:00,559
Are we sure about this?

572
00:33:00,684 --> 00:33:03,896
Wylie found a link through the cat blog
to an offshore account in Belize.

573
00:33:04,062 --> 00:33:07,316
It was hidden under aliases and shells
but he traced it back to Peterson.

574
00:33:08,275 --> 00:33:09,651
3.2 million bucks.

575
00:33:10,277 --> 00:33:13,947
You're accusing me...
get your people in line!

576
00:33:14,156 --> 00:33:15,199
Take him out of here.

577
00:33:16,241 --> 00:33:19,036
Abbott... You think I'm gonna
forget about this, huh?

578
00:33:19,495 --> 00:33:20,537
Is that what you think?!

579
00:33:21,038 --> 00:33:22,498
You have evidence
against Agent Peterson?

580
00:33:22,873 --> 00:33:25,209
You can pick up your firearms
on the way out. We're done here.

581
00:33:33,467 --> 00:33:35,177
- Bordick.
- Yeah?

582
00:33:36,220 --> 00:33:38,847
You look like you're in a hurry.
What's the rush?

583
00:33:39,264 --> 00:33:42,476
Nothing.
I mean none.

584
00:33:43,060 --> 00:33:44,895
You got a go-bag in your trunk,
don't you?

585
00:33:45,145 --> 00:33:46,313
What are you talking about?

586
00:33:47,481 --> 00:33:49,274
You killed Darrell Gonzalez.

587
00:33:50,943 --> 00:33:51,985
Where are you headed?

588
00:33:53,487 --> 00:33:55,405
The Gulf?
Airport?

589
00:33:56,615 --> 00:33:57,908
Why would I be going
to the Gulf?

590
00:33:58,075 --> 00:33:59,535
You killed Darrell Gonzalez.

591
00:34:03,288 --> 00:34:04,748
So you thought you were
gonna get away?

592
00:34:06,875 --> 00:34:07,918
Excuse me?

593
00:34:08,544 --> 00:34:11,588
When we arrested Peterson
you thought you had time to escape.

594
00:34:12,047 --> 00:34:14,341
- But I know what you did.
- What?

595
00:34:15,509 --> 00:34:19,263
- You killed Darrell Gonzalez.
- No. Peterson did.

596
00:34:20,264 --> 00:34:21,640
You guys said so.
You arrested him.

597
00:34:21,765 --> 00:34:24,351
It was you. I'm not letting
you alone until I prove it.

598
00:34:24,977 --> 00:34:26,770
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

599
00:34:27,229 --> 00:34:31,066
I am going to tail you every day
until you're in cuffs.

600
00:34:31,400 --> 00:34:32,901
I don't care how long it takes.

601
00:34:33,026 --> 00:34:35,028
I am gonna put you
behind bars.

602
00:34:40,409 --> 00:34:41,451
Lisbon.

603
00:34:49,835 --> 00:34:50,878
This is Abbott.

604
00:34:53,714 --> 00:34:54,756
Cho.

605
00:35:03,056 --> 00:35:04,099
Blanks.

606
00:35:26,038 --> 00:35:27,456
We found your go-bag.

607
00:35:27,789 --> 00:35:29,458
Yeah, quite the trip
you were planning.

608
00:35:29,958 --> 00:35:32,127
Fake passport,
Croatian Kunas.

609
00:35:32,294 --> 00:35:35,881
Hey, Lisbon, does Croatia
have an extradition treaty with the U.S.?

610
00:35:36,006 --> 00:35:37,591
I don't believe they do.

611
00:35:37,925 --> 00:35:42,387
We also found the tracking program
you installed on Gonzalez's computer.

612
00:35:43,138 --> 00:35:44,222
He'd suspected a mole.

613
00:35:44,348 --> 00:35:46,934
It was only a matter of time
before he latched on to you.

614
00:35:47,601 --> 00:35:49,728
So, why did you start working
for the Sosas?

615
00:35:50,604 --> 00:35:51,688
Why betray your team?

616
00:35:52,439 --> 00:35:53,482
My team?

617
00:35:54,441 --> 00:35:56,193
I've been at D.E.A.
for six years.

618
00:35:56,610 --> 00:35:59,446
You know how many times my "team"
has passed me over for promotions?

619
00:35:59,863 --> 00:36:01,949
So you wanted to show them
how smart you are?

620
00:36:02,199 --> 00:36:03,992
No, wait a minute.
He couldn't be that smart.

621
00:36:04,326 --> 00:36:05,452
I mean, we caught you.

622
00:36:06,787 --> 00:36:07,829
Took you years.

623
00:36:08,747 --> 00:36:14,211
That whole time, I was tipping off dealers
ruining busts, stashing payoffs.

624
00:36:15,212 --> 00:36:17,005
I was the most powerful guy
in that building.

625
00:36:17,798 --> 00:36:18,840
Nobody knew.

626
00:36:21,176 --> 00:36:22,219
So who's the smart one?

627
00:36:23,720 --> 00:36:26,181
Let's get this smart man
a nice jail cell.

628
00:36:34,815 --> 00:36:36,817
"We found enough evidence
in Orosco's apartment"

629
00:36:36,942 --> 00:36:39,277
"to arrest Korbell and several
of his employees."

630
00:36:40,862 --> 00:36:43,407
Korbell's gonna flip
against the Sosa cartel.

631
00:36:44,449 --> 00:36:45,826
Feels like a win,
all in all.

632
00:36:46,827 --> 00:36:49,371
You humiliated me
in front of my people!

633
00:36:49,496 --> 00:36:51,707
You perp-walked me
through my own office!

634
00:36:51,832 --> 00:36:54,418
We had to make Orosco feel like
he had a chance to get away.

635
00:36:54,543 --> 00:36:55,669
You were the misdirection.

636
00:36:55,794 --> 00:36:57,713
It's not the best part,
but you played it adequately.

637
00:36:57,838 --> 00:37:00,132
You were supposed to tell me
what you were doing.

638
00:37:00,257 --> 00:37:01,800
We couldn't do that.
You would have blown the shot.

639
00:37:01,967 --> 00:37:03,010
I mean, obviously.

640
00:37:03,135 --> 00:37:05,262
Look, I'm sorry, Bill.
Really, I am.

641
00:37:05,387 --> 00:37:08,056
I was supposed to get the credit!
We had a deal!

642
00:37:08,181 --> 00:37:09,433
There was no deal, Bill.

643
00:37:09,766 --> 00:37:11,643
Just a crazy idea you had
in your head.

644
00:37:11,810 --> 00:37:15,272
You're done, Abbott.
It's over for you and your wife.

645
00:37:15,397 --> 00:37:16,440
I'm gonna see to that.

646
00:37:16,565 --> 00:37:19,276
Okay. I've been patient.
I've been polite.

647
00:37:19,609 --> 00:37:20,902
Not anymore. Take it back.

648
00:37:23,363 --> 00:37:24,406
What?!

649
00:37:24,531 --> 00:37:28,076
Take back your little threat
and apologize to my friend here.

650
00:37:28,368 --> 00:37:29,411
Why?

651
00:37:29,995 --> 00:37:32,372
This display, this tantrum...

652
00:37:32,497 --> 00:37:34,916
it isn't about anger, is it?
It's about fear.

653
00:37:35,834 --> 00:37:37,377
Fear? Of what?

654
00:37:37,544 --> 00:37:40,797
That we weren't too far off about
you keeping a stash of dirty money

655
00:37:40,922 --> 00:37:43,050
and that with enough time,
we will find it.

656
00:37:47,220 --> 00:37:48,555
Give my best to Lena.

657
00:37:53,894 --> 00:37:56,480
- Are you sure about this?
- Absolutely.

658
00:37:56,938 --> 00:37:58,607
We have him
right where we want him.

659
00:37:59,900 --> 00:38:02,444
- No, I heard you were awesome down there.
- Really?

660
00:38:02,986 --> 00:38:05,822
Oh, because I felt like I was
gonna throw up the whole time.

661
00:38:05,947 --> 00:38:08,742
Lisbon said you nailed arresting Peterson.
Like a pro.

662
00:38:08,950 --> 00:38:11,286
- Well, it was actually fun.
- Yeah?

663
00:38:11,411 --> 00:38:14,581
I didn't think it would be,
but, uh, it was.

664
00:38:19,294 --> 00:38:21,838
- Oh, God.
- What?

665
00:38:24,382 --> 00:38:27,094
It's Bordick,
from San Antonio D.E.A.

666
00:38:27,636 --> 00:38:30,555
He's... asking me out.

667
00:38:32,849 --> 00:38:36,103
Fortunately, I can honestly
tell him I have no interest.

668
00:38:37,813 --> 00:38:40,774
I am so not into that right now.
I just wanna focus on work.

669
00:38:42,609 --> 00:38:43,652
Sure.

670
00:38:43,777 --> 00:38:46,071
- Know what I mean?
- Yeah. Totally.

671
00:38:46,863 --> 00:38:47,906
Me too.

672
00:38:48,865 --> 00:38:51,284
I am taking these files
down to admin.

673
00:38:51,701 --> 00:38:53,787
But will you be here later?

674
00:38:54,871 --> 00:38:55,997
Almost certainly.

675
00:38:56,706 --> 00:38:57,749
See you.

676
00:39:06,299 --> 00:39:07,425
The lights are a nice touch.

677
00:39:10,512 --> 00:39:13,348
- Happy Birthday.
- Thank you.

678
00:39:15,642 --> 00:39:16,685
Make a wish.

679
00:39:22,357 --> 00:39:24,818
And here is your gift.

680
00:39:30,240 --> 00:39:31,408
Open it.

681
00:39:47,382 --> 00:39:48,425
Lisbon.

682
00:39:49,843 --> 00:39:52,053
The one and only.
From the CBI.

683
00:39:52,888 --> 00:39:55,640
- You kept the pieces.
- Yeah.

684
00:39:56,183 --> 00:39:59,477
- Looks pretty nice, doesn't it?
- It's perfect.

685
00:40:00,896 --> 00:40:01,980
I'm speechless.

686
00:40:03,148 --> 00:40:04,191
It's...

687
00:40:04,524 --> 00:40:06,193
You really didn't know
what it was?

688
00:40:08,528 --> 00:40:09,988
Yeah, you can see for yourself.

689
00:40:17,078 --> 00:40:18,121
You really didn't know?

690
00:40:18,622 --> 00:40:20,707
I'm genuinely surprised.
This is...

691
00:40:25,045 --> 00:40:27,672
This is such a beautiful gift.
Thank you so much.

692
00:40:29,090 --> 00:40:30,133
I'm amazed.

693
00:40:32,177 --> 00:40:33,220
Bravo.

694
00:40:34,429 --> 00:40:35,555
Are you sure you're
not just pretending

695
00:40:35,680 --> 00:40:37,098
you didn't know what it was
to make me feel better?

696
00:40:37,224 --> 00:40:38,350
Because you don't have to make
me feel better.

697
00:40:38,475 --> 00:40:41,186
No, come on, please.
Lisbon, just take the compliment.

698
00:40:42,812 --> 00:40:43,855
Fine.

699
00:40:45,857 --> 00:40:47,943
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

